{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftusd\/capabilities"]},{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftusd\/capabilities"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"OpenUSD"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Capabilities","role":"article"},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/DifferencesInSwift","doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/CurrentLimitations"],"anchor":"Essentials"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/Capabilities","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Learn about the current capabilities of OpenUSD in Swift","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenUSD in Swift is currently evolving and may change in the future. Here are some key features currently supported:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Reference types in Swift","anchor":"Reference-types-in-Swift","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"UsdStage and SdfLayer are imported as classes in Swift and behave like classes written in Swift. When Swift passes a raw pointer to UsdStage or SdfLayer, Swift automatically increments or decrements the underlying reference count as needed, allowing Swift or C++ to influence the lifetime of the same UsdStage or SdfLayer."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["func makeTempStage() -> pxr.UsdStage {","    return Overlay.Dereference(pxr.UsdStage.CreateNew(\"\/tmp\/myStage.usda\", .LoadAll))","}","","func defineXform(_ stage: pxr.UsdStage, _ path: pxr.SdfPath) {","    stage.DefinePrim(path, .UsdGeomTokens.Xform)","}","","let stage = makeTempStage()","defineXform(stage, \"\/hello\")","let layer = Overlay.Dereference(stage.GetRootLayer())","layer.Save(false)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/WhatIsAForeignReferenceType","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/ForeignReferenceTypesAndSmartPointers","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for more information.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Warning","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When working in Swift, do not use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TfRefPtr.pointee"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TfWeakPtr.pointee"},{"type":"text","text":" to dereference Pixar’s smart pointers, as the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pointee"},{"type":"text","text":" property is unsafe. Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Overlay.Dereference(_:TfRefPtr)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Overlay.Dereference(_:TfWeakPtr)"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}]}],"style":"warning","type":"aside"},{"text":"Swift protocol conformances","anchor":"Swift-protocol-conformances","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Many OpenUSD types conform to one or more of the following protocols:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Identifiable"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomStringConvertible"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExpressibleByStringLiteral"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExpressibleByArrayLiteral"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragrap